// CF-1a refusal fixture / CF-1b acceptance fixture: the canonical
// guarded divide, the exact shape real shaders write.
//
// The then-arm value (0.25/uv.x) is computed, not provably finite.
// Executing both arms and blending arithmetically (slice B's select
// lowering: d = a-b; dst = cond*d + b) is NOT a conditional move —
// where uv.x <= 0.5 the untaken arm can produce inf/NaN and 0 * inf
// poisons the blend even though the arm "was not taken".  Purity
// excludes side effects; it does not exclude value contamination
// (design note §2 step 3, with the reference compiler's predicated
// emission as the settling evidence).
//
// CF-1a must therefore REFUSE this loudly on --general-lowering.
// CF-1b's predicated write (MOV default; CC-set from cond; CC-gated
// commit) lifts the refusal; its acceptance is the guarded-divide
// readback row judged in pixels (design note §5 tier c).
void main(float2 uv : TEXCOORD0,
          out float4 color : COLOR)
{
    float r;
    if (uv.x > 0.5f) {
        r = 0.25f / uv.x;
    } else {
        r = 0.0f;
    }
    color = float4(r, r, r, 1.0f);
}
